1
00:07:10,588 --> 00:07:16,588
A master director shining his light on the best rock band on the planet.

2
00:14:21,176 --> 00:14:27,176
Shine a Light is a documentary, music film directed by Martin Scorsese.

3
00:21:31,764 --> 00:21:37,764
Martin Scorsese’s electrifying concert documentary captures The Rolling Stones
live at New York’s Beacon Theatre during their A Bigger Bang tour.

4
00:28:42,352 --> 00:28:48,352
Filmed over two nights in 2006 with an all-star team of cinematographers, the film combines dynamic performances with archival
footage and rare glimpses behind the scenes, offering a vibrant portrait of the band’s enduring energy and legacy.

5
00:35:52,941 --> 00:35:58,941
Self - The Rolling Stones Vocals, Guitar, Harmonica, played by Mick Jagger.

6
00:43:03,529 --> 00:43:09,529
Self - The Rolling Stones Guitar, Vocals, played by Keith Richards.

7
00:50:14,117 --> 00:50:20,117
Self - The Rolling Stones Drums, played by Charlie Watts.

8
00:57:24,705 --> 00:57:30,705
Self - The Rolling Stones Guitar, played by Ronnie Wood.

9
01:04:35,294 --> 01:04:41,294
Self - The Rolling Stones Saxophone, Keyboards, played by Tim Ries.

10
01:11:45,882 --> 01:11:51,882
Self - The Rolling Stones Vocals, played by Blondie Chaplin.

11
01:18:56,470 --> 01:19:02,470
Shine a Light is a 2008 concert film directed by Martin Scorsese documenting the Rolling
Stones' 2006 Beacon Theatre performances during their A Bigger Bang Tour.

12
01:26:07,058 --> 01:26:13,058
The film also includes archive footage from the band's career and makes use of digital
cinematography  for backstage sequences, the first time Scorsese used the technology in a film.

13
01:33:17,647 --> 01:33:23,647
The film takes its title from the song of the same name,
featured on the band's 1972 album Exile on Main St.

14
01:40:28,235 --> 01:40:34,235
A soundtrack album was released in April 2008 on the Universal label.

15
01:47:38,823 --> 01:47:44,823
This is also the last movie by Paramount Classics, as the company merged into its
sister company Paramount Vantage after the movie was released.

16
01:54:49,411 --> 01:54:55,411
The film explores themes of new york city, concert,
rock 'n' roll, legend, movie business.
